    {
      "id": "hellmark-racing-cam",
      "title": "Hellmark's guide to the racing camshaft",
      "description": "Degreeing, lash, and break-in so a racing camshaft's extra lift turns into power.",
      "content": "A racing camshaft is only as strong as the way it is degreed in. Set the intake centerline on the marks, check the lash on a warm engine, and break the cam in at a steady rpm so the lifters pick up oil before the first hard pull.\n\nWith the valves opening farther and holding open longer, the same heads and carburetor move more air, and the engine makes more power upstairs.",
