      "id": "hellmark-racing-springs",
      "title": "Hellmark's guide to racing springs",
      "description": "Rate, ride height, and corner balance so racing springs keep the tire planted.",
      "content": "Racing springs keep the tire on the pavement when the car takes a set. Seat each spring square in its pocket, match the rates side to side, and check the ride height so one corner is not holding the car up alone.\n\nA stiffer rate resists dive and roll, so the contact patch stays flat through a corner instead of unloading the inside tire.",
