      "id": "hellmark-racing-shocks",
      "title": "Hellmark's guide to racing shocks",
      "description": "Rebound, compression, and heat care so racing shocks control the spring.",
      "content": "A racing shock keeps a stiff spring from bouncing the tire off the road. Set the rebound so the car settles once after a bump, and keep the compression firm enough that the nose does not dive the grip away on a hard stop.\n\nFresh fluid and sound mounts let that damping work at every corner instead of fading once the shock gets hot.",
